**Prefix and suffix stripping loops can cross and throw StringIndexOutOfBoundsException**

The `end` loop does not stop when it reaches `start`. When an illegal or redundant tag is adjacent to repeated characters—for example `<strong>{0}</strong></strong>` (which sanitizes to `<strong>{0}</strong>`) or `Hello <br>Hello` under `POLICY_NO_HTML` (which sanitizes to `Hello Hello`)—`start` and `end` overlap such that `start > sanitized.length() - end`. Line 111 then calls `sanitized.substring(start, sanitized.length() - end)` with `beginIndex > endIndex`, throwing a `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException`. Bound the `end` loop by `start`:
```java
while (end < sanitized.length() - start && end < value.length() - start && value.charAt(value.length() - end - 1) == sanitized.charAt(sanitized.length() - end - 1)) {
    end++;
}
```

