**`user != null` check disables conditional passkeys on initial login and ignores user credentials on re-authentication**

During initial login `context.getUser()` is `null`, so `user != null` evaluates to `false` and `webauthnAuth.fillContextForm(context)` is never called—breaking initial passkey authentication altogether. Meanwhile, when `user != null` (such as during re-authentication), it returns `true` even for users who have no passkey registered. Allow `user == null` for initial login and check whether the user has a passkey configured when `user != null`:

```java
protected boolean isConditionalPasskeysEnabled(UserModel user) {
    return webauthnAuth != null && webauthnAuth.isPasskeysEnabled()
            && (user == null || user.credentialManager().isConfiguredFor(webauthnAuth.getCredentialType()));
}
```

