**HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES are not filtered when searchQuery is empty**

Look at line 61 right above this: `if (!searchQuery) { return sorted; }` returns before your `!HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES.includes(attribute.name)` filter ever runs. By default, when the user has not typed a search query, `is_segment`, `project_id`, and `received` are still displayed and only vanish once the user starts searching. Filter `HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES` when building `sorted` before the `if (!searchQuery)` early return:

```tsx
const sorted = attributes
  .filter(attribute => !HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES.includes(attribute.name))
  .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
if (!searchQuery) {
  return sorted;
}
return sorted.filter(attribute =>
  attribute.name.toLowerCase().trim().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase().trim())
);
```

